structured_output_schema:
Structured output supports partial commits. Schema convention: top-level object includes __pragmas: {partial: boolean, fallback_trace: [string], committed_fields: [string]}. Example: {
  "user_intent": "create_event",
  "event": {
    "title": "Sync",
    "time": null
  },
  "__pragmas": {
    "partial": true,
    "fallback_trace": ["model_variant_small", "tool_simulated_timezone"],
    "committed_fields": ["title"]
  }
}

Guidelines: clients should render committed_fields confidently and surface uncommitted/null fields as placeholders. Console will index __pragmas for debugging and quality alerts. There will be an SDK helper to merge partial commits as they arrive.
